      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict confirmed_exact: position confirmed at this residue. validation_level surface_and_function -> function_only (paper reports surface: not_reported, function: yes). Paper (PMID 15269105): \"Of the 22 linker-inserted mutants, mutants InS(51), InV(139), InE(156), InS(493), InA(506), and InL(529) were fusogenic\". Audit note: Full text not readable: no PMC version, OUP page returns 403 to WebFetch and a Cloudflare bot check in the browser; only the abstract was read. Mutant name InV139 matches human canonical V139 (syncytin is a human protein, 538 aa), but whether the 5-aa linker sits before or after the named residue could not be checked; surface display not assessed in the abstract.] L5 explicitly names InV139 as a tolerated insertion in the SU subunit of full-length, membrane-anchored Syncytin-1. Residue 139 (V) is confirmed by code to lie in the extracellular domain (21-454), 316 residues from the TM boundary. Retained fusogenicity satisfies surface_and_function. residue_before=V (pos 139), residue_after=H (pos 140), read from the numbered sequence. Linker-scanning mutagenesis of full-length Syncytin-1 in 293T and HeLa cells; mutant InV139 (5-aa linker inserted after V139 in the SU subunit) was tested for fusogenic activity.",
